{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "our invoice-extraction agent (ADK, running on Cloud Run) is supposed to spit out JSON matching a pydantic InvoiceSchema but like 1 in 15 calls it comes back as ```json ... ``` or with a little 'Sure! Here's the extracted data:' preamble and json.loads blows up downstream. I've tried yelling at it in the instruction prompt, doesn't stick. Is output_schema on LlmAgent the right fix? I read it disables tools, and we need one tool call to look up vendor IDs first. Also should I be dropping temperature to 0 for this or is that not a thing anymore with the thinking models"},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Got an email from GCP saying the gemini model version we pin in prod is being retired next month. We've got ~8 ADK agents all hardcoding the model string. A few questions: (1) what's the sane replacement and do the thinking budget settings carry over or change, (2) can I set up an automatic fallback so if the primary model returns 429/503 we drop to a secondary model without the whole run failing, and (3) best way to centralize the model config so this isn't a find-and-replace job next time. Deadline is before the Nov 20 cutoff, so we'd like a plan this week."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "My ADK agent returns perfectly valid JSON now (finally) but when I deploy it to Agent Engine the response I get back from the remote app is wrapped in some event structure and my frontend can't find the fields. Locally with adk web it looks fine. What am I missing?", "needs_instead": "Help with deploying to Vertex AI Agent Engine and understanding/parsing the event stream and session response format returned by the remote agent API, not with model output formatting or model selection."}
]}
